## 1. SERP Intent Analysis

### 1a. Dominant Content Format

The top results are overwhelmingly **neighborhood listicles with descriptive sections per area**, structured as segmented guides rather than pure how-to content. Every competitor uses an H2-per-neighborhood format with prose descriptions covering lifestyle, housing type, price range, and commute. The format is consistent across apartment operators (Fairfield Residential), real estate agencies (VIP Realty, viprealestate.com), local moving companies (Colonial Van Lines), and lifestyle publishers (The Honest Local, theHonestlocal.com). This article must match that listicle-with-descriptive-sections format while differentiating on specificity, renter-focus, and information density.

Key structural pattern across top results: Brief intro (2-3 sentences) → neighborhood sections with sub-details → comparison element (some use tables) → brief closing. The writing agent must follow this macro-structure.

