The primary searcher is a **renter in the discovery or comparison stage of their housing search**: someone relocating to Houston for work (energy sector, Texas Medical Center, healthcare, aerospace), or a young professional or couple already in the city considering a neighborhood change. They are not yet searching for a specific apartment, but they are narrowing their geography. They want to understand how each neighborhood feels to live in, not just how it looks in a feature list. They expect a structured breakdown organized by lifestyle fit, with honest commentary on tradeoffs alongside the highlights, and at least approximate price reference points to calibrate their options.

